 "defect_observations": [
  "convolution-gamma-normal annex l.117 (\"The other order similarly gives G(z-x)\"), l.307 (\"The change y=zu, z>0, similarly gives\") and l.538-539 (\"the same argument with the variables interchanged\") remain in the routed read-only host; once routed, the owned lemmas thm:p15-w02c-p15-011-cdf-other-order, thm:p15-w02c-p15-011-beta-rescaling and thm:p15-w02c-p15-011-zero-variance-sum supply those steps, and the lead may wish to point the three sentences to them.",
  "convolution-gamma-normal annex l.388-398: the beta mean and variance follow \"Using the proved identity and the gamma recurrence\" and \"Subtracting the squared first moment\"; the intermediate algebra (B(alpha+1,beta)/B(alpha,beta)=alpha/(alpha+beta); alpha(alpha+1)/((alpha+beta)(alpha+beta+1))-alpha^2/(alpha+beta)^2=alpha*beta/((alpha+beta)^2(alpha+beta+1))) is not displayed. Compression only; both moments are displayed and the identities used are named.",
  "characteristic-functions-and-inversion body l.225-226 states the delta_0, a=0, b=1 endpoint example (limit 1/2 although mu((0,1))=0); the annex (l.395-397) writes only the a=-1, b=1 case. The a=0 case is an immediate instance of the proved inversion formula but is not written out.",
  "de-moivre-laplace-and-stirling annex l.191-195: the bound |E_{n,k}| <= (2/n^2) sum_{j<=k} j^2 is asserted from \"the logarithmic error bound\" without derivation; estimating log((n-j+1)/(n+j)) against -(2j-1)/n directly gives a larger constant. The conclusion E_{n,k}->0 uniformly for k<=M sqrt(n) is unaffected. Suspected constant slip, not a coverage gap.",
  "Owned body l.116-121 says the numerical constant of Feller's printed percentage bound (p.54) \"is obscured by a mark in the scanned copy consulted for this chapter and is not reproduced\". It records an unread source figure; it is not a pointer to an owed proof, but the author may be able to resolve it from the held page image."
